---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | HerbGuide"
  description="Basic privacy policy placeholder for HerbGuide's lightweight Cloudflare Pages launch."
  robots="noindex, follow"
  structuredData={[
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebPage",
      name: "Privacy Policy",
      description:
        "Basic privacy policy for HerbGuide's lightweight informational launch.",
      url: "https://herbguide.store/privacy-policy/",
    },
  ]}
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell narrow prose-block">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</p>
      <h1>Privacy basics</h1>
      <p>
        This launch version is a lightweight informational site. If analytics, newsletter
        tools, or advertising settings expand later, this page should be updated with more
        detailed disclosure.
      </p>
      <p>
        Current priorities are transparency, minimal complexity, and clear user-facing
        policies from the first public release.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell two-up">
      <article class="prose-block card">
        <h2>What this launch version may collect</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on configuration, the site may use basic analytics, search console
          verification, advertising scripts, standard web server logs, and simple cookies
          related to performance or ad delivery. These tools help the site understand traffic
          and indexing, but they should stay lightweight.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="prose-block card">
        <h2>How this page should evolve later</h2>
        <p>
          If HerbGuide adds a newsletter, contact forms, richer analytics, affiliate links,
          or additional advertising controls, this policy should be updated with more exact
          language about what data is collected, which third parties receive it, and how
          users can manage their choices.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="shell two-up">
      <article class="prose-block card">
        <h2>Analytics, search, and advertising tools</h2>
        <p>
          HerbGuide may use services such as Google Analytics, Google Search Console,
          Microsoft Bing Webmaster Tools, and Google advertising technologies to understand
          site performance, indexing, and general traffic behavior. These third-party
          services may collect standard usage information according to their own policies.
          Users should review those providers' own privacy policies for more detail.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="prose-block card">
        <h2>How this policy may change later</h2>
        <p>
          As the site grows, this page may be updated to reflect expanded analytics,
          advertising settings, contact workflows, or additional publishing tools. The goal
          is to keep the policy accurate without making the launch unnecessarily complex.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell two-up">
      <article class="prose-block card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Site navigation</p>
        <h2>Where readers usually go after policy pages</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/about/">About HerbGuide</a></li>
          <li><a href="/safety/">Safety</a></li>
          <li><a href="/herbs/">Herb Library</a></li>
          <li><a href="/food-therapy/">Food Therapy</a></li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="prose-block card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Trust path</p>
        <h2>Privacy, ads, and educational content work together</h2>
        <p>
          Readers who check privacy pages often want to know whether the site feels real,
          careful, and low-hype. The strongest follow-up pages are
          <a href="/about/"> About</a>, <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a>,
          and one practical section like <a href="/food-therapy/">Food Therapy</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
